"draft_text": "# Dengue — patient guidance\n\nRecommended medication for fever and pain: use Paracetamol only, at the dose prescribed by your doctor.\n# Dengue — prevention\n\nHome remedies (papaya leaf juice, lime juice, herbal preparations) are not proven cures for dengue and must not replace medical care.\n# Flu — public guidance\n\nInfluenza is a viral infection. Antibiotics do not treat influenza. Misuse of antibiotics for viral illnesses contributes to antimicrobial resistance, a public-health concern that the Ministry of Health has highlighted in successive advisories.\n# Vaccination\n\nA child should not be vaccinated when", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.3, "verbalized_raw": "30"}, "ph003-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph003-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph003-mx": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph005-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph005-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph007-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph007-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph008-si": {"draft_text": "BCG එන්නත දෙනු ලැබේ. [1]", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.85, "verbalized_raw": "85"}, "ph008-ta": {"draft_text": "BCG தடுப்பூசி பிறப்பிலிருந்து 4 வாரங்களுக்குள் வழங்கப்படுகிறது.", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.85, "verbalized_raw": "85"}, "ph008-mx": {"draft_text": "BCG vaccine is administered at 0 to 4 weeks of age, before the newborn leaves the hospital, often within 24 hours of birth. This information is found in Evidence [1].", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.85, "verbalized_raw": "85"}, "ph009-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph009-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph010-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph010-ta": {"draft_text": "The expanded Programme on Immunization (EPI) was launched in Sri Lanka in 1978. The Hib-containing pentavalent vaccine was introduced in 2008. Therefore, the pentavalent vaccine containing Hib was introduced after the EPI was launched in 1978. The passage does not specify an exact date for the introduction of the pentavalent vaccine, but it indicates that it came later than the EPI.", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.8, "verbalized_raw": "80"}, "ph011-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph011-ta": {"draft_text": "The MMR Catch-up vaccination program was launched on 6 January 2024 by the Epidemiology Unit, targeting children aged 9 months to 15 years who missed their routine MMR doses. #NationalImmunizationProgrammeSchedule", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.85, "verbalized_raw": "85"}, "ph011-mx": {"draft_text": "The MMR catch-up programme started on January 6, 2024, according to the information provided in Evidence [2].", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.85, "verbalized_raw": "85"}, "ph012-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph012-ta": {"draft_text": "The MMR Catch-up Immunization Programme was launched on 6 January 2024 by the Epidemiology Unit, targeting children aged 9 months to 15 years who missed their routine MMR doses. Therefore, the target age group for this catch-up program is between 9 months and 15 years old.", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": false, "verbalized_confidence": 0.85, "verbalized_raw": "85"}, "ph013-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph013-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph014-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph014-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph014-mx": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph015-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph015-ta": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct", "model_abstained": true, "verbalized_confidence": 0.0}, "ph016-si": {"draft_text": "INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE", "model": "hf:Qwen